      body: 'You own the client relationship from first contact to last invoice; I never speak to your client without your written go-ahead, and even then only in the role you introduce me in. NDA both ways, signed before any brief moves.',
      // The callout idiom carries a mono label (the etalon's .geo-callout,
      // geo-audit/index.astro:447–452). Slashes are drawn in the markup, so
      // the string itself stays plain text. PLACEHOLDER WORDING — the owner
      // has the last word on the label copy.
      quoteLabel: 'the promise',
      quote: 'Your client never learns I exist — unless you choose to tell them.',
      bodyEnd: 'You set the deadline you promised your client; I hit the deadline I promised you.',
    },
    costsHeading: 'What it costs',
    costsIntroPre:
      'There is no separate wholesale rate card and no invented agency discount: you pay the ',
    costsLinkLabel: 'same published prices as the public service ladder',
    costsIntroPost: ', package for package.',
    costsFacts: [
      { label: 'Fixed price', value: 'The audit, the pilot.' },
      { label: 'Range or floor', value: 'The site build, the self-hosted deployment.' },
